[free_text]
# Two string fields are new in the answer of host/computer/appInput (answers of server requests are walked by free_text_fields.json).
# src/free_text.rs: next to `(Kind::Answer, "host/computer/appInput", ...)` if a row exists, else next to
# `(Kind::Answer, "host/computer/command", &["/text", "/error"])` add
#     (Kind::Answer, "host/computer/appInput", &["/text"]),
# tests/it/free_text_fields.json: `"answer host/computer/appInput /text"` goes into the `free` class (the one that holds
# `answer host/computer/command /text`), and `"answer host/computer/appInput /code"` into the `refused` class whose reason starts
# "a kind, mode, scope, phase, sort, state or other word from a fixed vocabulary" (next to `answer host/computer/appInput /effect`).
# The params (core -> host request) are not walked.

